MEMOIRS OF THE THIRD HOKAGE
Hiruzen Sarutobi, Sandaime Hokage — Personal Reflections (Archived)

"They called me the God of Shinobi and the Professor, for it was
said I had mastered every jutsu in the village. Titles are heavy
things. I served two terms, the second taken up after the Fourth
gave his life to seal the Nine-Tails.

My students — Jiraiya, Tsunade, and Orochimaru — the Legendary
Sannin, were my greatest pride and my deepest grief. That one of
them turned to darkness is a wound I carry.

A village is a family. Every child of the leaf is my grandchild.
If there is a lesson I would leave, it is this: those who abandon
their comrades are worse than trash. Protect the Will of Fire, and
pass it to the next generation."

Hiruzen Sarutobi fell defending the village during the Konoha Crush,
sealing away the Second Hokage's and First Hokage's reincarnated arms
and the arms of Orochimaru at the cost of his life.
